A measurement budget follows the whole equation (@gas-measurement-budget: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @industrial-gases-and-vacuum, #source "../sources/Ionization-Gauge-Calibration-Fedchak.lingua#r_18KG5KWT64MPYQ4D47V1T99CKW", #source "../sources/Gas-Flow-Standards-NIST.lingua#r_2FJV0VJ3K710PNV7E45JGGJXG5", #industrial-gases-and-vacuum "../../../inquiry/metrology/practice/Conformity-and-risk.lingua#r_41AJHYZ4Q8B821Z892PNNK1MEJ") { r_43CV8XW3GA858G802Y97M2DWJ5
**Read:** [Calibration of ionization vacuum gauges — Fedchak and colleagues](../sources/Ionization-Gauge-Calibration-Fedchak.lingua#r_18KG5KWT64MPYQ4D47V1T99CKW), uncertainty and reporting; [Gas flow standards and their uncertainty — Wright and colleagues](../sources/Gas-Flow-Standards-NIST.lingua#r_2FJV0VJ3K710PNV7E45JGGJXG5), complete example budgets; use the shared covariance treatment.

Start from the measurement equation and the definition of the result. Include reference values, calibration coefficients, response, environment, sampling, gas state and model discrepancy where they affect that equation. A list of instrument accuracy numbers is not yet an uncertainty budget.

For p=I/(K Ie), the first-order relative variance contains the squared relative contributions with signs determined by the derivatives, plus covariance terms. A common calibration can cancel in one ratio and reinforce another. Repeated observations reduce only the contributions justified by their dependence structure.

For a pressure difference Δp=p₁−p₂ measured with a common additive offset, that offset cancels if it is truly unchanged. A drifting offset or shared multiplicative scale behaves differently. Carry the actual model rather than choosing correlation coefficients because they make the answer smaller.

**Work:** Construct a budget for one gauge comparison and one collected-flow result. Check derivatives with independent finite perturbations, then compare linear propagation with a nonlinear simulation where warranted. Report standard versus expanded uncertainty and the basis of the coverage claim; a small uncertainty cannot repair a wrong measurand or model.

**Return:** [Industrial gases, vacuum and high-purity supplies — from molecules to useful service](../Industrial-gases-and-vacuum.lingua#r_3GHQJEYMYEN6JDKSF4PPJ403RF).
